{{also|menage|Menage|ménagé}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|menage}}
* {{alter|en|menâge||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|ménage}}; compare {{cog|enm|menage}}, a parallel borrowing from an earlier form of the French word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mɛˈnɑːʒ/|/meɪˈnɑːʒ/|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːʒ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|household or domestic situation}} A [[household]]; a [[domestic]] situation. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Lady Anne Granard|page=167|volume=I|passage="Oh," cried her ladyship, "I see the whole '''''ménage'''''; they will take a first floor over a baker's shop, to save fire, and live upon red herrings during the week, with a mutton chop by way of meat on a Sunday."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1939|author=w:Raymond Chandler|title=The Big Sleep|page=39|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2011
|passage=It smelled of ether and something else, possibly laudanum. I had never tried the mixture but it seemed to go pretty well with the Geiger '''''ménage'''''.}}
# {{senseid|en|ROSCA in Scotland}} {{lb|en|now|_|Scotland}} A type of [[cooperative]] society whereby all members pay a regular sum of [[savings]], or through which goods can be paid for in [[installment]]s. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{hyper|en|ROSCA}}
# {{senseid|en|group for sex or group sex}} A group of people in a [[sexual]] relationship; especially, such a group that live together; the relationship itself. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#: {{hypo|en|ménage à trois|ménage à quatre|ménage à moi}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=aeegmn|Meegan|manege|manège}}

